# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dataset documentation for the SIMULATED hypertension trial data.
# The object itself lives in data/sim_htn_trial.rda and is generated by
# data-raw/sim_htn_trial.R. Nothing here comes from real patients.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

#' Simulated hypertension trial data (3000 synthetic participants)
#'
#' @description
#' **THIS IS SIMULATED DATA.** `sim_htn_trial` was generated entirely by a
#' parametric simulation (seed 20261105) to serve as a single, self-contained
#' example dataset for every function in macodgent. It contains no real
#' patients, no real trial results and no personally identifiable information.
#' All estimates, p values and survival probabilities printed in the package
#' examples are artefacts of the simulation and must not be interpreted as
#' clinical evidence. Do not use this dataset for clinical, regulatory or
#' epidemiological inference.
#'
#' The simulated design is a two-arm, five-site hypertension trial with a
#' baseline visit and three follow-up visits, a laboratory panel, a binary
#' blood-pressure-control endpoint, an ordinal blood-pressure grade, a
#' time-to-cardiovascular-event endpoint with death as a competing cause, and
#' a matched case-control substructure for conditional logistic regression.
#'
#' The object carries provenance attributes: `attr(d, "simulated")` is `TRUE`,
#' `attr(d, "seed")` is 20261105, and `attr(d, "provenance")` repeats the
#' synthetic-data warning. `comment(d)` holds the same warning.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 3000 rows and 47 columns:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{id}{integer. Unique synthetic participant identifier (1-3000).}
#'   \item{site}{factor, 5 levels. Simulated recruiting centre.}
#'   \item{match_id}{integer. Matched-pair identifier for conditional logistic examples.}
#'   \item{treatment}{factor: Placebo / Active. Simulated random allocation.}
#'   \item{dose_level}{ordered factor: Low / Medium / High.}
#'   \item{sex}{factor: Female / Male.}
#'   \item{race}{factor, 3 levels. Anonymous simulated group label.}
#'   \item{education}{ordered factor: Basic / Secondary / Tertiary.}
#'   \item{age}{numeric, years.}
#'   \item{bmi}{numeric, kg/m2.}
#'   \item{waist_cm}{numeric, cm.}
#'   \item{smoke}{factor: No / Yes. Current smoking.}
#'   \item{alcohol}{factor: No / Yes.}
#'   \item{exercise_hours}{numeric, hours per week.}
#'   \item{salt_g_day}{numeric, grams per day.}
#'   \item{diabetes}{factor: No / Yes.}
#'   \item{dyslipidemia}{factor: No / Yes.}
#'   \item{ckd}{factor: No / Yes. Chronic kidney disease.}
#'   \item{prior_cv}{factor: No / Yes. Prior cardiovascular event.}
#'   \item{family_history}{factor: No / Yes.}
#'   \item{sbp_baseline}{numeric, mmHg. Baseline systolic pressure.}
#'   \item{dbp_baseline}{numeric, mmHg. Baseline diastolic pressure.}
#'   \item{sbp_week4}{numeric, mmHg. Week-4 systolic pressure.}
#'   \item{sbp_week8}{numeric, mmHg. Week-8 systolic pressure.}
#'   \item{sbp_week12}{numeric, mmHg. Week-12 systolic pressure (continuous endpoint).}
#'   \item{dbp_week12}{numeric, mmHg. Week-12 diastolic pressure.}
#'   \item{heart_rate}{numeric, beats per minute.}
#'   \item{ldl}{numeric, mg/dL. LDL cholesterol.}
#'   \item{hdl}{numeric, mg/dL. HDL cholesterol.}
#'   \item{triglycerides}{numeric, mg/dL. Right-skewed.}
#'   \item{glucose}{numeric, mg/dL. Fasting glucose.}
#'   \item{creatinine}{numeric, mg/dL.}
#'   \item{egfr}{numeric, mL/min/1.73m2. Estimated glomerular filtration rate.}
#'   \item{potassium}{numeric, mmol/L; contains missing values.}
#'   \item{sodium}{numeric, mmol/L.}
#'   \item{crp}{numeric, mg/L. Strongly right-skewed inflammatory marker.}
#'   \item{urine_albumin}{numeric, mg/g; right-skewed, contains missing values.}
#'   \item{adherence_pct}{numeric, 0-100; contains missing values.}
#'   \item{quality_score}{numeric, 0-100; contains missing values.}
#'   \item{bp_control}{factor: No / Yes. Binary week-12 control endpoint.}
#'   \item{bp_grade}{ordered factor: Normal / Elevated / Stage 1 / Stage 2.}
#'   \item{adverse_event}{factor: No / Yes.}
#'   \item{compliance}{ordered factor: Low / Medium / High.}
#'   \item{followup_days}{numeric, days to event or administrative censoring at 730 days.}
#'   \item{cv_event}{integer 0/1. Cardiovascular event indicator for Cox / KM examples.}
#'   \item{comp_event}{integer 0/1/2. 0 censored, 1 cardiovascular event, 2 death (competing cause).}
#'   \item{case_status}{integer 0/1. Matched case-control indicator for clogit examples.}
#' }
#'
#' @details
#' Missingness is simulated as MCAR on `potassium`, `quality_score`,
#' `adherence_pct` and `urine_albumin` so that `mc_impute_knn()` and
#' `mc_impute_mice()` have a realistic target. Correlations among blood
#' pressure, anthropometric and laboratory variables are built in so that
#' `mc_correlate()`, `mc_pca_regression()` and the penalised regressions have
#' a non-degenerate structure. Treatment effects on blood pressure and on the
#' event hazard are deliberately small and synthetic.
#'
#' @source
#' Fully synthetic. Generated by `data-raw/sim_htn_trial.R` in this package
#' with `set.seed(20261105)`. No external data source, no real patient data.
#'
#' @examples
#' # SIMULATED DATA -- 3000 synthetic hypertension-trial participants.
#' # Not real patients; see ?sim_htn_trial. Every macodgent example uses it.
#' data(sim_htn_trial)
#' d <- sim_htn_trial
#' dim(d)                       # 3000 rows, 47 columns
#' attr(d, "simulated")         # TRUE
#' attr(d, "provenance")        # synthetic-data warning
#' head(d[, c("id", "treatment", "sbp_baseline", "sbp_week12", "bp_control")])
"sim_htn_trial"
